# Test-only overlay on the root policy (which still applies — see
# InheritParentConfig). Tests are held to the same bug/UB/lifetime bar as src.
InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access

# Why: clang-tidy cannot see through Catch2's REQUIRE. After
# `REQUIRE(x.has_value());` the very next `*x` is reported as unchecked access,
# because REQUIRE expands to a macro that throws rather than to an `if`. It is a
# WarningsAsErrors check, so every optional-returning API under test would have
# to be re-asserted with a hand-written `if (!x) { FAIL(); return; }`. The
# assertion IS the check; the checker just cannot read it.
